{"term":"plight","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:5f81c9c6984411dd9b","definition":"A dire or unfortunate situation.","example":"Though we say we are quite clear about it and understand when someone uses the expression, unlike that other expression, maybe we're in the same plight with regard to them both.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plight#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5f1af8b22a53202696","definition":"A (neutral) condition or state.","example":"although hee live in as good plight and health as may be, yet he chafeth, he scoldeth, he brawleth, he fighteth, he sweareth, and biteth, as the most boistrous and tempestuous master of France[…].","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plight#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:718f481f42dfa22b29","definition":"Good health.","example":"All wayes shee sought him to restore to plight, / With herbs, with charms, with counsel, and with teares[…].","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plight#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d7d6c984fd99ec58a4","definition":"Responsibility for ensuing consequences; risk; danger; peril.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dialectal","register":"dialectal","wordFamily":["plightful","plightless","plightly","plighty","replight","trothplight","unplight"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plight#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:29ab296fce49e9a62a","definition":"An instance of danger or peril; a dangerous moment or situation.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dialectal","register":"dialectal","wordFamily":["plightful","plightless","plightly","plighty","replight","trothplight","unplight"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plight#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:295f6fce296c7de491","definition":"Blame; culpability; fault; wrong-doing; sin; crime.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dialectal","register":"dialectal","wordFamily":["plightful","plightless","plightly","plighty","replight","trothplight","unplight"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plight#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e5c06709bed79587a9","definition":"One's office; duty; charge.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dialectal","register":"dialectal","wordFamily":["plightful","plightless","plightly","plighty","replight","trothplight","unplight"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plight#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2ec140459d32d01627","definition":"That which is exposed to risk; that which is plighted or pledged; security; a gage; a pledge.","example":"Haply, when I shall wed,\nThat lord whose hand must take my plight shall carry\nHalf my love with him, half my care and duty","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic","wordFamily":["p